### Lot 3 demo, organizer and point-of-sale side: cash code at a till, walk-up sale + print, block/refund, till
### close 10 DH short, Encaissements and B3 figures (IntelliJ HTTP client).
#
# Start the backend with the dev profile (dev seed: ATLAS FC with cash points, admin +212600000001; dev enables the
# simulated card gateway, wallet and cash network):
#   docker compose up -d && SPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE=dev ./gradlew bootRun
# Make the event and the fan cash code with lot1-sale.http first (steps 1-8), then pay with
#   POST /fan/orders/{id}/pay {"method": "CASH_AGENCY"}  -> pay_code (put it in @payCode)
# A second code can be paid on the simulated agent terminal instead: open {{base}}/payments/cash/fake in a browser.
# OTP codes are printed by the dev log sender ([dev OTP] +2126... -> 123456): paste into @orgCode / @cashierCode.

@base = http://localhost:8080/v1
@org = a7a5fc00-0000-4000-8000-000000000001
@adminPhone = +212600000001
@cashierPhone = +212633333333
@walkUpPhone = +212644444444
@orgCode = 000000
@cashierCode = 000000
@eventId = 1
@priceId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@payCode = 4F7K29
# Local dates, both included (the server turns them into instants with its own tzdata); at most 92 days.
@from = 2026-11-01
@to = 2026-11-07
@timezone = Africa/Casablanca

### 1. Admin: ask for a code
POST {{base}}/org/auth/otp
Content-Type: application/json

{"phone": "{{adminPhone}}"}

### 2. Admin: verify
POST {{base}}/org/auth/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{"phone": "{{adminPhone}}", "code": "{{orgCode}}"}

> {% client.global.set("orgToken", response.body.token); %}

### 3. Admin: a cashier (OTP login, no PIN). Again with the same phone -> 422 TAKEN.
POST {{base}}/org/staff
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Nadia Guichet", "role": "CASHIER", "phone": "{{cashierPhone}}"}

### 4. Cashier: ask for a code
POST {{base}}/org/auth/otp
Content-Type: application/json

{"phone": "{{cashierPhone}}"}

### 5. Cashier: verify
POST {{base}}/org/auth/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{"phone": "{{cashierPhone}}", "code": "{{cashierCode}}"}

> {% client.global.set("cashierToken", response.body.token); %}

### 6. Cashier: open the till (201; already open -> 200 with it)
POST {{base}}/org/pos/sessions
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"label": "Guichet Nord"}

> {% client.global.set("sessionId", response.body.id); %}

### 7. Cashier: look the fan's code up (case, spaces, hyphens and the JMH prefix are ignored; O reads 0)
GET {{base}}/org/pos/codes/jmh-{{payCode}}
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}

> {% client.global.set("amount", response.body.amount_mad); %}

### 8. Cashier: "Encaisser" the exact amount -> PAID + tickets; the fan's WhatsApp delivery row is queued
POST {{base}}/org/pos/codes/{{payCode}}/collect
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"amount_mad": {{amount}}}

### 9. Cashier: walk-up sale of 2 places; the 2nd holder has no phone (paper only)
POST {{base}}/org/pos/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"sale_id": "{{$random.uuid}}", "event_id": {{eventId}}, "items": [{"price_category_id": "{{priceId}}", "qty": 2,
  "holders": [{"name": "Salma Bennani", "phone": "{{walkUpPhone}}"}, {"name": "Karim Tazi"}]}]}

> {% client.global.set("saleId", response.body.id); %}

### 10. Cashier: print data, one 80 mm slip per ticket (qr = static v1 token; every call is an audited print)
GET {{base}}/org/pos/orders/{{saleId}}/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}

> {% client.global.set("ticketA", response.body.tickets[0].id); client.global.set("ticketB", response.body.tickets[1].id); %}

### 11. Cashier: the running figures (collected_mad so far)
GET {{base}}/org/pos/session
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}

### 12. Admin (or OPS): block one ticket -> BLOCKED in the next manifest version
POST {{base}}/org/tickets/{{ticketA}}/block
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"reason": "Démo blocage"}

### 13. Admin: refund another ticket -> REFUNDED, place back on sale, a REQUIRED refund
POST {{base}}/org/tickets/{{ticketB}}/refund
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"reason": "Démo remboursement"}

### 14. Refunds to do (REQUIRED first)
GET {{base}}/org/refunds?status=REQUIRED&event_id={{eventId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}

> {% client.global.set("refundId", response.body[0].id); %}

### 15. Admin or FINANCE: money given back by hand -> DONE with a reference
POST {{base}}/org/refunds/{{refundId}}/done
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"reference": "Caisse club 0001"}

### 16. Cashier: close the till declaring 10 DH less than expected (expected 15000 if steps 8 + 9 only)
POST {{base}}/org/pos/sessions/{{sessionId}}/close
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"declared_mad": 14000}

### 17. B8 Encaissements (ADMIN, OPS, FINANCE; CASHIER -> 403): per day x collector, sessions with the gap
GET {{base}}/org/finance/cash?from={{from}}&to={{to}}&timezone={{timezone}}
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}

### 18. Same as CSV (; separated, UTF-8 BOM, CRLF, amounts like 1250,50)
GET {{base}}/org/finance/cash.csv?from={{from}}&to={{to}}&timezone={{timezone}}
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}

### 19. B3: awaiting_cash, methods (every payment method, zeros included), refunded, refunded_mad
GET {{base}}/org/events/{{eventId}}/sales
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
